/**
 * mh-conditions.mjs — content for the mental-health condition explainer pages.
 *
 * These are the "understanding-<condition>.html" pages: plain-English, non-diagnostic
 * explainers of anxiety, depression, OCD, panic attacks, social anxiety and chronic
 * stress/burnout. They sit alongside the screener and city pages, share the same page
 * shell (mh-pages.mjs) and are generated by build-mh-pages.mjs.
 *
 * Tone rules, same as everywhere else in this folder:
 *  - nothing here is a diagnosis, and we say so on every page;
 *  - the only crisis number quoted is Tele-MANAS (14416);
 *  - no statistics are invented — where a page needs a number it stays qualitative;
 *  - each page leads with explanation, offers a free self-check, and only then a session.
 *
 * `check` is a data-ll-open id that exists in lume-wellbeing-check.js. There is no
 * OCD/panic/social-anxiety-specific scale, so those pages point at the GAD-7 anxiety
 * check (gad7) or the full menu (wellbeingMenu); the copy never claims the check
 * measures the condition itself.
 */

